diff --git a/tests/ms178/README.md b/tests/ms178/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..d275142d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/ms178/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,112 @@
+# ms178 host regression and stress harness (v3)
+
+These tests use the actual production C implementations with mocked kernel calls.
+They are **not** GPU, game, firmware, display-hotplug, or whole-kernel tests.
+Assertions are forced on, even if the production build uses NDEBUG.
+
+## Normal execution
+
+On Linux with AMDGPU and Meson tests enabled, all eight test executables are
+registered in `ms178-host` and run with the regular Meson tests:
+
+```sh
+meson test -C build-llvm23 --print-errorlogs
+meson test -C build-llvm23 --suite ms178-host --print-errorlogs
+```
+
+The standalone runner supports an existing configured tree and GCC or Clang:
+
+```sh
+CC=/path/to/llvm23/bin/clang CONFIG_DIR=build-llvm23 \
+ UBSAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=1 \
+ SANITIZE_FLAGS='-fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-omit-frame-pointer' \
+ sh tests/ms178/run-host.sh
+```
+
+Executables use a unique temporary directory, cleaned on exit. Set TEST_OUTPUT
+to a custom prefix to retain them. Sanitizers are separate runs, not combined:
+
+- ASan+UBSan: `-fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-omit-frame-pointer`
+- TSan: `-fsanitize=thread -fno-omit-frame-pointer`
+- MSan (Clang): `-fsanitize=memory -fsanitize-memory-track-origins=2 -fPIE -pie`
+
+The MSan result concerns this host harness/intercepted libc paths; it does not
+make the system libraries or GPU driver stack fully memory-instrumented.
+
+## Deeper deterministic stress
+
+```sh
+MS178_STRESS_ROUNDS=3000 MS178_VA_STEPS=500000 \
+ UBSAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=1 \
+ meson test -C build-asan --suite ms178-host --num-processes 1 \
+ --timeout-multiplier 3 --print-errorlogs
+```
+
+- `host.c`: original randomized VA invariants, four-thread internal VA stress,
+  overflow, fixed placement, BO handle-table bounds/growth and public VA calls.
+- `mock.c`: raw CS and BO-list thresholds, dependency and semaphore packing,
+  successful semaphore consumption, fence waits, allocation and ioctl errors,
+  full CPU mapping span and reference ownership.
+- `kms.c`: full-width IDs, last-write-wins and KMS copy/OOM smoke tests; its
+  optional CLI also supplies an instrumented CPU-only commit microbenchmark.
+- `sync.c`: real fd duplication success and EBADF propagation.
+- `kms-stress.c`: eight threads with separate requests and independent latest-
+  value oracles, boundary sizes, rewind/restore, duplicate, self/other merge,
+  caller immutability, every reached commit/duplicate allocation failure,
+  growth failure and ioctl errors. Default 300 rounds/thread; deep 3000.
+- `va-stress.c`: bitmap oracle for exact address selection, not just nonoverlap;
+  arbitrary alignment, top/bottom and fixed requests, full hole conservation;
+  eight seeds (default 50,000 transitions/seed, deep 500,000). Public frees
+  under total malloc failure and 80,000 concurrent public alloc/free pairs.
+- `device.c`: real duplicated /dev/null fds with mock DRM responses; version,
+  fd and mutex failures, query errors, authenticated dedup migration/refcounts,
+  independent device handles and /proc/self/fd conservation.
+- `queries.c`: query/count/pointer guards, exact VM/MMR wire layout, mocked GFX9
+  initialization and oversized pre-GFX9 shader-engine bounds, path/token/name
+  parsing. No real GPU query results are assumed.
+
+## Sensitivity, coverage and proofs
+
+```sh
+python tests/ms178/mutations.py --cc /path/to/llvm23/bin/clang --out /tmp/mutations
+python tests/ms178/coverage.py --out /tmp/coverage
+python tests/ms178/proofs.py
+```
+
+Mutation tests intentionally edit production files and then restore them.
+**Run only in a disposable tree, never concurrently with builds or tests.**
+All ten mutants must fail at runtime; compilation failures do not count.
+Coverage requires GCC/gcov; it reports uncovered changed lines and branches,
+not merely a favorable percentage. Proofs require Python z3-solver and prove
+only the documented arithmetic/layout identities, not lifetime or races.
+
+## CPU-only performance replay
+
+Reconstruct each comparison source from its pinned patch/base, configure the
+v3 build-llvm23 tree, then:
+
+```sh
+python tests/ms178/perf-matrix.py \
+ --source main=/path/to/pristine-main --source v1=/path/to/v1 \
+ --source v2=/path/to/v2 --source v3=/path/to/v3 \
+ --cc /path/to/llvm23/bin/clang --out /tmp/perf-results
+```
+
+Nine repetitions, rotating version order, one allowed logical CPU, identical
+`-O3 -march=raptorlake` compilation. Includes sorted/reverse/random requests,
+63/64/65 boundaries, old-capacity history, generic/pow2 VA and fragmentation,
+and public VA batch release. Allocation counters and VA output hashes are
+recorded. Report absolute times and losses as well as wins. Batch mean time
+is **not a p99 frame-time metric**. Do not run other builds during measurement.
+
+`mca.py` accepts the saved production VA assembly and verifies instruction
+presence before running LLVM-MCA 23.1.6 with the Raptor Lake model. It models
+arithmetic slices only, excluding guards, loops, locking, syscalls and GPU work.
+
+## Limits
+
+Passing these tests does not establish production readiness on the user's GPU.
+The report includes uncovered cumulative error paths, the unavailable 32-bit
+build, unresolved cold upstream diagnostics, and the physical-hardware gate.
+Do not apply failed mutants or deploy GCC coverage/ASan/TSan/MSan builds as a
+performance build. Never use mock-test profiles as representative gaming PGO.
diff --git a/tests/ms178/coverage.py b/tests/ms178/coverage.py
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..836f4984
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/ms178/coverage.py
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""GCC/gcov branch+line evidence for host tests, including uncovered lines."""
+import pathlib,subprocess,argparse,gzip,json,re,csv,os
+p=argparse.ArgumentParser();p.add_argument('--out',required=True);p.add_argument('--config',default='build-llvm23');a=p.parse_args();r=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];out=pathlib.Path(a.out).resolve();out.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
+for name in ['host','mock','kms','sync','kms-stress','va-stress','device','queries']:
+ d=out/name;d.mkdir(exist_ok=True);exe=d/name
+ cmd=['gcc','-std=c11','-UNDEBUG','-D_GNU_SOURCE','-O0','-g','--coverage','-ffunction-sections','-fdata-sections','-include',str(r/a.config/'config.h'),'-I'+str(r),'-I'+str(r/'include/drm'),'-I'+str(r/'amdgpu'),str(r/f'tests/ms178/{name}.c'),'-pthread','-Wl,--gc-sections','-o',str(exe)]
+ subprocess.run(cmd,check=True,cwd=r)
+ with (d/'run.log').open('w') as f:subprocess.run([str(exe)],stdout=f,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,check=True,cwd=r)
+ for gcno in d.glob('*.gcno'):
+  with (d/'gcov.log').open('a') as f:subprocess.run(['gcov','-j','-b','-c',str(gcno)],stdout=f,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,check=True,cwd=d)
+ exe.unlink()
+counts={};branches={}
+for pth in out.rglob('*.gcov.json.gz'):
+ data=json.loads(gzip.decompress(pth.read_bytes()))
+ for f in data['files']:
+  src=pathlib.Path(f['file']);src=src if src.is_absolute() else r/src
+  try:rel=str(src.resolve().relative_to(r))
+  except ValueError:continue
+  for line in f['lines']:
+   k=(rel,line['line_number']);counts[k]=counts.get(k,0)+line['count']
+   for i,b in enumerate(line.get('branches',[])):branches[(rel,line['line_number'],i)]=branches.get((rel,line['line_number'],i),0)+b['count']
+changed=set();file=None;line=0
+patch=subprocess.check_output(['git','diff','libdrm-v1-upstream','--unified=0','--','*.c','*.h'],cwd=r,text=True)
+for s in patch.splitlines():
+ if s.startswith('+++ b/'):file=s[6:]
+ elif s.startswith('@@'):
+  m=re.search(r'\+(\d+)',s);line=int(m.group(1))
+ elif s.startswith('+') and not s.startswith('+++'):
+  if file and not file.startswith('tests/'):changed.add((file,line))
+  line+=1
+ elif not s.startswith('-') and not s.startswith(('diff ','index ','---')):line+=1
+with (out/'changed-lines.csv').open('w') as f:
+ w=csv.writer(f);w.writerow(['file','line','execution_count','instrumented'])
+ for k in sorted(changed):w.writerow([*k,counts.get(k,0),'yes' if k in counts else 'no'])
+summary={}
+for file in sorted(set(k[0] for k in changed)):
+ lines=[k for k in changed if k[0]==file and k in counts];br=[k for k in branches if (k[0],k[1]) in changed and k[0]==file]
+ summary[file]={'instrumented_added_lines':len(lines),'executed_added_lines':sum(counts[k]>0 for k in lines),'added_line_branch_outcomes':len(br),'hit_branch_outcomes':sum(branches[k]>0 for k in br)}
+(out/'summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary,indent=2)+'\n');print(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))
+print('Coverage is host-path coverage, not a correctness proof; uncovered lines are retained.')
